more_disgraceful	two	disgraceful	P3	more shameful by the standard just agreed, i.e. exceeding in pain or evil (S11, S15)	more shameful in common opinion, as "you and the world" agree, i.e. worse in repute
more_painful	one
more_evil	one
# more_evil: "evil" as a measure of the fine (S1, S7: useful to anyone, e.g. to spectators or the city) may differ from evil to the doer, which C needs in order to answer Polus at S18. The text never says whose evil is meant in P1 or C, so I left it as one sense.
